"termsAndConditions_description" = "Dear User,\nWelcome to the products and/or services provided by ECBOT Limited (together, “ECBOT,” “we,” “us”) through this tongue imaging app and its extensions (the “Service”). We place a high priority on protecting the security and privacy of your personal information and are committed to applying appropriate safeguards to protect it.\nThis Privacy Policy applies to all information you provide when you access and use the Service and any related products and services. It explains how we collect, use, store, share, transfer, and protect your personal information, and the rights and options you have to access, correct, delete, withdraw consent, and close your account.\nPlease read this Privacy Policy carefully. By using the Service, or continuing to use it after we update this Privacy Policy (we will notify you as required), you are deemed to have read and agreed to the updated Privacy Policy and authorize us to process your information as described herein.\n\nPersonal Information Protection Principles We Follow\n	•	Definition of Personal InformationPersonal information refers to various types of information recorded electronically or otherwise that can identify a specific natural person, either alone or in combination with other information, or reflect the activities of a specific natural person.\n	•	Compliance and LegalityWe comply with applicable laws and standards, including the Cybersecurity Law of the People’s Republic of China, the Personal Information Protection Law of the People’s Republic of China, and GB/T 35273-2020. We collect and use personal information based on the principles of lawfulness, fairness, necessity, and good faith.\n	•	Expanded Purposes (Notice and Consent)If we need to use your personal information for purposes not described in this Privacy Policy, or apply the collected information in new scenarios, we will provide reasonable and clear notice and obtain your explicit consent where required.\n	•	De-identification/Anonymization and Data AnalysisWhere appropriate, we may de-identify information so it cannot be used to identify you. De-identified/anonymized data is generally not considered personal information under applicable law. Without disclosing your personal information, we may conduct aggregated analysis to improve services and support business and operational decisions.\n	•	Sharing of Aggregated StatisticsWe may share anonymized or aggregated statistical information with the public or third parties to show overall usage trends. Such information will not include details that identify you.\n\nOverview of Key Topics\n	•	Collection and use of personal information\n	•	Sharing, transfer, and public disclosure of personal information\n	•	Storage, retention, and protection of personal information\n	•	Cookies and other tracking technologies\n	•	Your rights and choices\n	•	Protection of minors’ personal information\n	•	Updates to this Privacy Policy\n	•	How to contact us\n	•	Dispute resolution\n\n1. Collection and Use of Personal Information\nWe collect and use personal information only as necessary to provide and improve the Service in accordance with applicable law.\n1.1 Account Registration\nTo register an account, you may register using your email, mobile phone number, Apple account or gmail account. If you do not provide the required information, you may be unable to complete registration or use certain functions.\n1.2 Image-Based Feature Analysis\nTo use certain image-based functions, we may request camera permission so you can capture and upload images. If you do not grant this permission, you may not be able to use those image-based functions, but this will not affect other unrelated features.\nWe may process uploaded images to identify and describe visual characteristics (e.g., color, texture, and other observable features) and generate a summary or report for display in the Service. Image quality may be affected by lighting, angle, and device conditions.\n1.3 Information Obtained Indirectly\nIf you log in through third-party platforms (such as gmail), we may receive certain account information you authorize the third party to provide (e.g., nickname, avatar).Where permitted by law and with your authorization as required, we may also receive information from affiliates, partners, or service providers to support Service operation.\n1.4 Exceptions Where Consent May Not Be Required\nWhere permitted by applicable laws and regulations, we may collect and use personal information without prior consent in circumstances including:\n	•	national security and national defense;\n	•	public safety, public health, or major public interests;\n	•	criminal investigation, prosecution, trial, and enforcement;\n	•	to protect vital lawful rights and interests where consent is difficult to obtain;\n	•	information you disclose publicly;\n	•	information obtained from lawful public sources;\n	•	necessary for concluding or performing a contract at your request;\n	•	necessary to maintain the safe and stable operation of products/services (e.g., troubleshooting);\n	•	legitimate news reporting;\n	•	statistics/research in the public interest with de-identification applied;\n	•	other circumstances provided by law.\n1.5 Questions About Legal Basis\nIf you have questions about the legal basis for our processing, please contact us using the details in Section 8.\n\n2. Rules for Sharing, Transfer, and Public Disclosure\n2.1 Sharing of Personal Information\nWe do not share your personal information with any company, organization, or individual outside ECBOT unless:\n	•	we obtain your explicit consent;\n	•	required by laws/regulations or competent authorities;\n	•	necessary to provide functions you request (we will provide notice and obtain consent where required);\n	•	sharing with affiliates: with your consent and where appropriate, we may share de-identified/anonymized data with our affiliates for service improvement, product development, market research, and data analysis. If an affiliate changes the purpose of processing, it must obtain your authorization again where required.\nWe may share necessary information with authorized partners to provide the Service (only within the scope stated in this Privacy Policy), such as:\n	•	communications, logistics, payment service providers for order processing, delivery, and payment confirmation;\n	•	promotion/marketing partners, using non-identifying aggregated or indirect data for performance analysis (without disclosing personally identifiable information).\n2.2 Transfer of Personal Information\nWe do not transfer your personal information except:\n	•	with your explicit consent; or\n	•	in merger, division, acquisition, reorganization, or liquidation scenarios—where we will require the recipient to continue to be bound by protections no less than this Privacy Policy; otherwise, we will seek consent again where required.\n2.3 Public Disclosure\nWe publicly disclose personal information only when:\n	•	you give explicit consent;\n	•	required by law/regulations or legal proceedings; or\n	•	we receive a legally binding request and disclose as required by law.\n2.4 Sharing/Transfer/Public Disclosure Without Prior Consent\nWhere permitted by law, we may share/transfer/disclose without prior consent under situations such as those listed in Section 1.4.\nFor properly anonymized/de-identified data that cannot be re-identified by the recipient, sharing/transfer/public disclosure may not require further notice or consent as permitted by law.\n\n3. Storage, Retention, and Protection Measures\n3.1 Storage and Retention Period\nDuring your use of the Service, unless you delete information or disable collection via system settings (where applicable), we will retain the personal information you provide or generate for as long as necessary to provide the Service and fulfill the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, unless a longer retention period is required by law.\n3.2 Protection of Personal Information\n3.2.1 Security Measures\nWe adopt security measures consistent with industry standards, including:\n	•	reasonable technical and organizational measures to prevent unauthorized access, disclosure, use, alteration, damage, or loss;\n	•	encryption and security mechanisms to protect confidentiality and integrity;\n	•	access controls and confidentiality obligations for personnel with authorized access;\n	•	regular security and privacy training;\n	•	data minimization and timely deletion once retention is no longer necessary or lacks legal basis.\n3.2.2 Safety Reminders\n	•	No internet transmission is completely secure; avoid sending sensitive personal information via unencrypted channels.\n	•	Do not upload or share information you consider highly sensitive.\n	•	Do not disclose financial account numbers, bank cards, credit cards, third-party payment accounts, or passwords through the Service.\n	•	In cases of impersonation or misuse of others’ identities, we may delete relevant information and restrict access as appropriate.\n3.2.3 Security Incident Response\n	•	We maintain incident response plans for vulnerabilities, malware, and cyberattacks.\n	•	If a personal information security incident occurs, we will notify affected users as required by law, including the incident overview, potential impact, measures taken, and recommended protective steps. Notification may be by email, letter, phone, push notification, or public announcement when individual notice is impractical.\n	•	If you believe your information may be at risk, contact us using Section 8.\n\n4. Cookies and Other Tracking Technologies\nWe may use cookies or similar technologies (e.g., device identifiers) to support Service functionality and improve user experience. We do not use cookies for purposes beyond those described in this Privacy Policy.\n4.1 Security and Operational Performance\nWe may use security/authentication cookies or identifiers to help verify login security, prevent fraud, and optimize performance.\n4.2 Convenience and User Experience\nThese technologies may help reduce repeated input and maintain preferences (e.g., one-click login, saving certain usage settings).\n\n5. Your Rights and Choices\nSubject to applicable laws and regulations, you have the following rights:\n5.1 Access and Correction\nYou may access and correct your personal information. For changes to important information (e.g., mobile number, gmail binding), we may re-verify identity for security.If you cannot access or correct through normal channels, contact us and we will respond within 30 business days after verification.\n5.2 Deletion\nYou may request deletion by contacting us. After verification, we will process deletion. You may request deletion where:\n	•	processing violates laws/regulations;\n	•	we processed without required consent;\n	•	we breached an agreement with you;\n	•	you stop using the Service or close your account;\n	•	we cease operations.\nWhere applicable, we will also notify relevant third parties that received your information from us to delete it, unless otherwise required by law or independently authorized by you. We will respond within 30 business days after receiving a verified request.\n5.3 Device Permission Management\nYou can disable device permissions (e.g., notifications, photos, camera) in your device settings at any time. Disabling permissions may affect certain functions.\n5.4 Account Closure\nYou can request account closure via the contact method in Section 8. After verification, we will close your account and stop providing services, and delete your personal information as required, unless retention is required by law.\n5.5 Obtain a Copy of Your Information\nYou may request a copy of your personal information. After verification, we will respond within 30 days. Where technically feasible, we may transfer a copy to a third party designated by you upon request.\n5.6 Withdraw Consent\nYou may withdraw consent by contacting us. After verification, we will process within 30 business days. Withdrawal may affect functions that require the relevant information. Withdrawal does not affect processing already performed based on prior consent, to the extent permitted by law.\n\n6. Children’s Personal Information\n	•	The Service is primarily intended for adults. Minors should not create accounts without the consent of a parent or legal guardian.\n	•	We treat individuals under 14 as children and apply enhanced protections in accordance with applicable laws.\n	•	If we discover we collected children’s information without valid guardian consent, we will delete it as soon as practicable.\n\n7. Updates and Notices\n	•	We may revise this Privacy Policy from time to time. Please review updates carefully. Continuing to use the Service after an update means you accept the revised Privacy Policy.\n	•	We will not reduce your rights under this Privacy Policy without your explicit consent. Updates will be posted on this page.\n	•	For material changes, we will provide more prominent notice (e.g., in-app notice or pop-up).\n	•	Material changes may include:\n	•	changes to purposes/types/methods of processing;\n	•	significant corporate restructuring (merger, acquisition, bankruptcy, etc.);\n	•	changes to sharing/transfer/public disclosure recipients;\n	•	significant changes to your rights or how you exercise them;\n	•	changes to the responsible department/contact/complaint channels;\n	•	high-risk findings in impact assessments.\nIf you do not accept updates, stop using the Service.\n\n8. Contact Us\nIf you have any questions, comments, suggestions, or complaints about this Privacy Policy or personal information processing, contact:\nEmail: ecbot602@gmail.com";
